    <!-- Body -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Finding the breaker for an outlet is a two-minute job with the right tool and a twenty-minute job without one. Either way, the answer is not finished until you have switched that breaker off and proved the outlet is dead, because outlets are fed in more creative ways than panel labels admit.
        </p>

        <TopPick />

        <div id="before" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Before You Start
          </h2>

          <p>
            First, check the outlet works. Plug in a lamp or a phone charger with a light. If it is dead already, look for a tripped GFCI outlet nearby (bathrooms, kitchens, garages, outdoors and basements usually have one that protects others downstream), check for a wall switch that controls the outlet, and look at the panel for a breaker sitting in the tripped middle position.
          </p>

          <p>
            If the outlet is dead because a breaker tripped, reset it by pushing it firmly off and then on. If it trips again straight away, leave it off. Something on that circuit is faulting, and repeated resets are a bad idea. That is a job for an electrician, not a labelling exercise.
          </p>

          <p>
            Check the panel labels, but do not trust them. Labels are often original, vague and out of date. Treat a label as a starting guess that tells you where to look first.
          </p>

          <p>
            Open only the outer panel door. All four methods below work with the inner dead-front cover in place. Removing it exposes live bus bars and is never necessary for this job. If the panel looks scorched, smells hot, buzzes or is wet, stop and call a licensed electrician before touching anything.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Method</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Time</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">People</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best for</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Breaker finder</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">2-5 min</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">1</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Any live outlet, mapping many outlets</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Lamp or radio with helper</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">5-15 min</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">2</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">No finder, a phone and a helper</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Solo elimination</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">10-30 min</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">1</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">No finder, no helper</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Electrician with tracer</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">One visit</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Pro</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Dead outlets, odd wiring</td>
